qa#1 · os-justin · session_01QSeKYpxQpmErd1ixfkgbYh

**Priority note and one addition** 2026-11-18T01:23Z, on the maintainer's word in the verification seat's session, verbatim: 「三个问题 同意」. The three answers were: no self-approval default; the confirmation gate is not widened to `update_record`; the HTTP door's elicitation (#34321) stays on hold.

- **Why this card comes first among the scorer items:**
  - on the open HTTP door a confirmed write cannot land (`no_confirmation_service`, #33689, `ai-service.ts`);
  - so an agent that follows the gate scores 0 on that turn;
  - an agent that routes around it with a raw `update_record` and writes the target state may score;
  - the card's second turn is graded on the target state only (`packages/qa/scenarios/README.md`).

  The second point is read from the grading rule and not yet confirmed on a runner record. Until this lands, model comparisons on operations reward bypassing the gate.
- **Addition to the scope:** the scenario build prompt (`packages/qa/scenarios/src/runner/prompts.ts`, the "confirm first" line) also asks the build to lock the field that a gated action changes. That matches the skills card filed today from the same answer. Without it, a card's build leaves the bypass open.
- #34214 touches the same grading files; keep the two serial.
